1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,790
Charles Darwin once said “A man who dares to waste one hour of time has not discovered the value of life”.
查尔斯·达尔文曾说过：“敢于浪费一小时时间的人，还没有发现生命的价值。”

2
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:16,830
If you live one hundred years, that only equates to twelve-hundred months – and when you break it down even further into days, hours and minutes, it gets more frightening.
如果一个人能活一百年，那也只相当于一千二百个月——再进一步把它拆解成日、时、分，这个数字会更令人心惊。

3
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:18,580
Why is this relevant?
这一点有什么意义呢？

4
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:22,630
Well, quite simply put: life is short.
道理很简单：人生苦短。

5
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:28,780
Spending eight hours every day in a slumber means you’re losing a third of your life to bed.
每天花八个小时睡觉，意味着你有三分之一的生命都在睡梦中度过。

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:35,040
So, the question is: is eight hours the exact amount we need, or is it just a myth?
那么问题来了：八小时睡眠是我们所需的准确时长，还是只是一个固有说法？

7
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:43,030
While most scientists agree that between seven and nine hours a night is the optimal amount, this is just a rough estimate.
尽管大多数科学家都认同每晚七到九小时是最佳睡眠时长，但这只是一个粗略的估算。

8
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:46,210
In truth, it’s a little more complicated than that.
事实上，实际情况要比这复杂一些。

9
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:52,350
It seems that the amount of sleep you need depends upon your age – with infants needing much more than adults.
一个人需要的睡眠时长似乎取决于年龄——婴儿需要的睡眠时间远多于成年人。

10
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:57,730
What does seem apparent is that around seven and a half hours’ sleep is a good amount.
有一点似乎很明确：每晚大约七个半小时的睡眠是比较合适的。

11
00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:04,510
In a study conducted at the University of Surrey Sleep Research Centre, the effects of sleep were monitored.
萨里大学睡眠研究中心开展了一项研究，监测了睡眠带来的影响。

12
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:08,940
One group slept for six and a half and the other for seven and a half hours per night.
研究人员将受试者分为两组，一组每晚睡六个半小时，另一组睡七个半小时。

13
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:20,020
While some findings were predictable – irritation and lower concentration in the group who slept less, there were some more surprising findings. The genes of people who had less sleep were affected.
一些研究结果在意料之中——睡眠不足的一组出现了易怒、注意力下降的情况，但还有一些结果更令人惊讶：睡眠不足者的基因受到了影响。

14
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:25,800
Genes associated with inflammation, the immune system and stress response became more active.
与炎症反应、免疫系统和应激反应相关的基因变得更加活跃。

15
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:32,190
The team also observed increases in the activity of genes related to diabetes and risk of cancer.
研究团队还发现，与糖尿病和癌症风险相关的基因活性也有所上升。

16
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:37,340
One of the biggest issues is that myths regarding sleep are constantly perpetuated.
关于睡眠的错误观念一直在被不断传播，这是最棘手的问题之一。

17
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:42,350
For example, have you ever heard that you can train yourself to need less or no sleep?
比如，你有没有听过这种说法：你可以训练自己适应更少的睡眠，甚至不睡觉？

18
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,940
It’s simply not true.
这纯属无稽之谈。

19
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:59,480
We will always need a certain amount of sleep – eight hours might not be the exact sweet spot, and there are factors like age to take into consideration, but one thing is true – there is a certain amount we do actually need.
人类始终需要一定时长的睡眠——八小时或许并非精准的理想时长，而且还有年龄等因素需要考虑，但有一点是毋庸置疑的：我们确实需要充足的睡眠。
